{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "002B", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\emptyset$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b75750d760531005fd2771c7fcb3f425ae7d32b6ba21da5f32177ebde51402f9", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a2f7f605ae1fe3dc7c37176ee2236816f4a313d44111d5ce54de9fdf0c82a513", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nIn the category of sets the empty set <MATH_0001> is an\ninitial object, and in fact the only initial object.\nAlso, any <TEXTITOPEN_0001>singleton<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>, i.e., a set with one element,\nis a final object (so it is not unique).", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a54dadd5a113d238d33d3a63fe1635f7970474b408206ccda0b8e27f9d1407bb", "unit_id": "tag:002B:paragraph-0001"}
